# Commit the curated memory and the record of what was explored; ignore bulk
# model output and machine-local runtime state.
#
# From logs/, these go to git:
#   runs.jsonl    the run records — provenance for every reported number
#   brief-*.md    the briefs sent to each debate seat. Small (tens of KB for a
#                 whole project) and they are the written record of which
#                 directions were proposed and attacked, which is what a
#                 coauthor means by "did we ever explore X". They are useless
#                 sitting on one person's laptop.
#
# The debate log stays local: it carries full model responses and gets bulky,
# and the briefs plus state.md's changelog already carry what a coauthor needs.
#
# Note the rule shape: git cannot re-include a file whose parent DIRECTORY is
# ignored, so this must be `*/logs/*` plus negations, never `*/logs/`.
*/logs/*
!*/logs/runs.jsonl
!*/logs/brief-*.md

# Per-author runtime state: machine-local, and meaningless to anyone else.
# `python` in particular holds an absolute venv path.
*/run
*/round
*/python

# machine-local: this clone has been through onboarding
*/onboarded
